Atlas overlay patch 0098: ui/rest-mark
Why: scene 9 of the reel ("Tabs you are not using rest", still full-66): in the sidebar a tab that
gave its memory back has a dim title and a frost mark (the WolOS glyph weather-snow, accent) at the
right of its row, the tab in front never; one click wakes it. Memory Saver and the discarding are the
engine's (inherited series); this is the picture. The logic and the glyph are new files
(chrome/browser/ui/atlas/rest/rest_mark.*, rest/vector_icons); the row view gets three hooks: the
title colour, the mark painted over the row where the close button of the tab in front sits, and a
colour update when the discard state changes. No setting draws a row, so hook lines are the
smallest tier. Integration stand-in for the rest area (numbers 0024-0029 stay free for it).
Files: chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/common/tab_view.{h,cc}
Test filter: *AtlasRestMark*; reel-check scene R09 (5 resting rows dim with the mark, the selected one never)
Rebase risk: M (tab_view.cc is also hooked by the sidebar patches 0021/0022; three small hunks)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

